inv.notes:
Key flags for the orchestrator:

(1) Item 015 is not simply applicable to LootHistory, because the addon has no AceDB profile surface at all (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:289, docs/schema.md:7). Adding /lh profile <name> either (a) switches a vestigial profile that changes nothing, (b) answers a fixed "no profiles" line, or (c) is omitted and recorded as a Documented-deviations row. Per CLAUDE.md this must be surfaced to the user as a deviation decision, not decided silently.

(2) If a profile verb is added anywhere in the suite, check whether the standard or LibKa0s reserves it. lib.LIVE_VERBS (libs/LibKa0s/Slash.lua:113-116) does not include it, so the verb would be refused while the addon is disabled. tests/test_disabled.lua:395-410 forbids widening LIVE_WHILE_DISABLED away from the library's set, so a collection-wide profile verb likely wants an upstream LibKa0s/standard change first (a new LIVE_VERBS member plus the slash-commands-§2 text), then a re-vendor.

(3) If the verb is added, insertion position is constrained by tests/test_diagnostics.lua:303 (diagnostics must directly follow debug). Also add it to UNAVAILABLE_WITHOUT_LIB (settings/Slash.lua:314) if it should not be offered degraded.

(4) Smoke doc defects to fix during 010:
- the suite index is missing §17 and §19;
- the broken #11-minimap-button anchor;
- a doubled "---" at :1387-1389;
- "the 17 scenarios" at :1450;
- the §6a "mapID not exported" statement at :361 contradicts §17i.4 at :1216-1218 (export carries mapID);
- the §9 /lh list row enumeration at :583-585 lists 9 rows, but docs/module-map.md:163 says the schema has seventeen rows (stale);
- §17b.4 at :1010 says "each of the four pages", but there is one sub-page now (§9 :517);
- §17a.8 at :985 says "/lh (the help)", which conflicts with bare /lh opening config.

(5) Keep docs/debug.md:44 and :151 in sync with any renumbering. Those are the only live section-number references outside the file.

(6) Keep the resetall-is-non-destructive statement, which the ARCHITECTURE.md:328 deviation row cites.

(7) The 1500-line cap applies (the file is at 1465), so consolidation should shrink it.

inv.smoke_tests_pinning:
tests/test_doc_structure.lua:334-384, test "docs/smoke-tests.md carries a non-English-client section" (:353). It reads docs/smoke-tests.md and captures from the first heading matching `[Nn]on%-English client` (LOCALE_HEADING :351) down to the next heading of the same or higher level. It asserts that:
- the heading exists (:365);
- the section contains "deDE" or "frFR" (:370);
- the section contains one of "Failure"/"failure"/"Fail"/"the finding" (FAILURE_WORDS :352, assertion :374-380);
- the section is at least 10 lines long (:382).
A regroup must keep a heading with the words "Non-English client", naming deDE/frFR, with failure wording and 10 or more lines. Nesting it under a higher-level theme heading is fine as long as its own heading still matches.

The shared kit prose gate (tests/_kit/test_prose.lua:5-6, :316-320) scans every .md under docs/, smoke-tests.md included, for banned words and British spellings. The rewrite must pass it.

No other test counts the file's headings, IDs or sections. test_doc_structure.lua:204 only resolves anchors that point INTO ARCHITECTURE.md, so the SMK-F001 anchor in ARCHITECTURE.md:198 is not checked mechanically.

One test parses the file: tests/test_doc_structure.lua:344-404, test "docs/smoke-tests.md carries a non-English-client section" (:363). It reads docs/smoke-tests.md and captures the section under the first heading matching `[Nn]on%-English client` (LOCALE_HEADING :360) up to the next heading of the same or higher level. It asserts:
(a) such a heading exists (:375);
(b) the section contains "deDE" or "frFR" (:380);
(c) the section contains one of FAILURE_WORDS {"Fail","failure","Failure","the finding"} (:361, :384-390);
(d) the section is at least 10 lines (:392);
(e) the section contains the literal "C_SpellBook.IsSpellKnown" (:397-403). That means the §7a IsSpellKnown check, or at least a mention of it, must stay inside the non-English section. If §7a and §12b are deduped, the IsSpellKnown text has to live under the locale heading, or the test must be updated.
It does not pin numbering, section count or anchors. Its name is listed in the generated docs/test-cases.md:850.

Indirect coverage: the kit prose gate tests/_kit/test_prose.lua (scope at :5-6, :316-320) scans every docs/*.md, so rewritten smoke prose must pass the banned-word lists. Waivers are in tests/prose_waivers.lua, which has no smoke-tests entry today (:26 waives only data-flow.md). tests/_kit/test_eol.lua checks line endings on all tracked files. No test counts smoke checks or headings.
